/* book: lead: A strain gauge is a resistor glued to a part. When the part stretches or compresses, the resistor changes resistance in proportion to the strain. The constant of proportionality is the gauge factor. This simple idea turns a mechanical quantity into an electrical one. Engineers use it for load cells, pressure diaphragms, torque shafts and displacement beams. It also measures bone strain, implant lo */
